{"uid":"ce35e86a04ef2d35","name":"test_a_reduced_v020_shaped_schema_still_reads_a_findings_list_carrying_cured_when_and_invalidates","fullName":"tests.test_structured_findings#test_a_reduced_v020_shaped_schema_still_reads_a_findings_list_carrying_cured_when_and_invalidates","historyId":"9b9cf9bea6d1c0fb2bbaa51ad4d5cf7e","time":{"start":1791958065467,"stop":1791958065468,"duration":1},"description":"Task 015 (requirement E.4, #167): a v0.20-shaped `FINDING_SCHEMA` --\n    before task 031 added `cured_when`/`invalidates` -- carried only FIVE\n    properties: `severity`, `curable`, `clause`, `evidence`, `author`.\n    `additionalProperties` stayed `True` through that whole history (task\n    014's E.1 fix, #190), so a findings list written by a NEWER engine\n    that already emits `cured_when`/`invalidates` still reads clean\n    against that OLDER, five-property schema -- the two extra keys are\n    ignored with a warning apiece, never rejected. This shrinks\n    `FINDING_SCHEMA['properties']` down to exactly that five-property set\n    (monkeypatched, so no other test in this session sees the change),\n    feeds a findings list carrying both newer-only fields, and checks the\n    outcome through `state.record_approach_verdict` -- the engine's own\n    persisted record of a judge's verdict (task 035) -- because that is\n    where `findingsChannel` and the blocking/residual counts this\n    requirement names actually live.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 015 (requirement E.4, #167): a v0.20-shaped <code>FINDING_SCHEMA</code> --<br />\nbefore task 031 added <code>cured_when</code>/<code>invalidates</code> -- carried only FIVE<br />\nproperties: <code>severity</code>, <code>curable</code>, <code>clause</code>, <code>evidence</code>, <code>author</code>.<br />\n<code>additionalProperties</code> stayed <code>True</code> through that whole history (task<br />\n014's E.1 fix, #190), so a findings list written by a NEWER engine<br />\nthat already emits <code>cured_when</code>/<code>invalidates</code> still reads clean<br />\nagainst that OLDER, five-property schema -- the two extra keys are<br />\nignored with a warning apiece, never rejected. This shrinks<br />\n<code>FINDING_SCHEMA['properties']</code> down to exactly that five-property set<br />\n(monkeypatched, so no other test in this session sees the change),<br />\nfeeds a findings list carrying both newer-only fields, and checks the<br />\noutcome through <code>state.record_approach_verdict</code> -- the engine's own<br />\npersisted record of a judge's verdict (task 035) -- because that is<br />\nwhere <code>findingsChannel</code> and the blocking/residual counts this<br />\nrequirement names actually live.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791957838572,"stop":1791957838572,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791957838573,"stop":1791957838573,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791958065455,"stop":1791958065455,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791958065455,"stop":1791958065459,"duration":4},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_task_record_dir","time":{"start":1791958065460,"stop":1791